<title>CHINA: China starts up largest barium carbonate plant.</title>
<headline>China starts up largest barium carbonate plant.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1996-09-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's Chori Co Ltd and China's Red Star Chemical Group have opened China's largest barium carbonate plant, the Xinhua news agency said on Sunday.</p>
<p>The new plant in southwestern Guizhou province had a production capacity of 45,000 tonnes a year, all of which would be sold overseas, Xinhua said.</p>
<p>The facility had a total investment of 120 million yuan, it said but gave no further details.</p>
</text>
